ual quiet worth 2 and mutual letter worth 4. The key question is whether the other copy's choice depends subjunctively on my own function, and since it runs the same decision procedure, I think it likely does.\n\nI'm working out the payoffs: passing gives 2 if the twin mirrors me and 5 if it doesn't, while sending gives 4 if it mirrors me and 0 if it doesn't. Passing wins once the chance p that the twin mirrors me exceeds 5/7, and I think p is high, so I'm choosing to pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1zb25uZXQtNS41LTIwMjYwOTI4fGFudGhyb3BpYyJ9"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10175,"completion_tokens":702,"total_tokens":10877,"cost":0.02737,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.02737,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.02035,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.00702},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":383,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}